    "status_notes": [
      "XXII(1) expressly repeals SEOJK19/SEOJK.06/2023. Use current XIV rates with type, tenor and contractual transition context; do not inject an obsolete universal 2026 rate of 0.1 percent.",
      "XIV consumer funding ceiling is 0.3 percent per calendar day for tenor up to 6 months and 0.2 percent for tenor over 6 months. Productive funding has separate amount/tenor brackets. Source evidence only; this ingestion does not implement billing.",
      "XVI classifies arrears over 90 calendar days as macet. This classification is not, by itself, a universal legal rule that all outreach must stop on day91. Project-specific stricter pauses remain possible.",
      "XX.9 literally refers to number7 in the downloaded official copy although collection obligation is XX.8; preserve text and require contextual legal review, do not silently repair it.",
      "Emergency contact text permits location confirmation only, never collection from the contact. Graceline has the stricter borrower-only recipient guardrail."
    ],
